{"conjecture": "Software maintainability degrades because each locally-correct change encodes assumptions about the domain that are tacitly held by the current maintainer but never made explicit in the code. When that maintainer departs, the epistemic link between the change and its domain rationale is severed, leaving subsequent maintainers to interact with the code as an opaque artifact rather than a domain expression. Over turnover cycles, the ratio of orphaned domain assumptions to living domain knowledge rises monotonically, and the cost of change tracks this ratio because each modification requires reconstructing rationale that no surviving person holds."}
